      The primary purpose of setting clocks forward is to shift the artificial hours of light on civil clocks so that they better align with peak human wakefulness. The SVG illustration below demonstrates how advancing the clock by one hour transfers daylight from early morning to evening.
    </p>

    <div style="margin: 2.5rem 0; text-align: center; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 800 280" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block; margin: 0 auto;">
        <rect width="800" height="280" fill="#0f172a" rx="10" />
        <text x="400" y="30" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="16" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">Daylight Re-allocation under Standard Time vs DST</text>
        
        <!-- Timeline Background -->
